      "hints": [
        "Set $2x + 1 = \\tan^{-1}(1/3) + k\\pi$.",
        "For $x > 0$, choose $k = 1$ ($x \\approx 1.23$) and $k = 2$ ($x \\approx 2.80$)."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Isolate the trigonometric term and take the inverse tangent:\n$$3\\tan(2x + 1) = 1 \\implies \\tan(2x + 1) = \\frac{1}{3}$$\n$$2x + 1 = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\approx 0.32175\\text{ radians}$$",
        "Since $x > 0 \\implies 2x + 1 > 1$, add integer multiples of $\\pi$ to obtain valid positive arguments:\n$$2x_1 + 1 = 0.32175 + \\pi \\approx 3.46334 \\implies 2x_1 = 2.46334 \\implies x_1 \\approx 1.2317 \\approx 1.23\\text{ radians}$$\n$$2x_2 + 1 = 0.32175 + 2\\pi \\approx 6.60494 \\implies 2x_2 = 5.60494 \\implies x_2 \\approx 2.8025 \\approx 2.80\\text{ radians}$$\n$$(\\text{Smallest two positive values: } x = 1.23, \\quad 2.80)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Trigonometric Equations": "Takes $\\tan^{-1}(1/3) \\approx 0.322$ (M1). Adds $\\pi$ and $2\\pi$ (DM1). Obtains $x = 1.23$ (A1) and $x = 2.80$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
