      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the identity $\\sin^2 x = 1 - \\cos^2 x$ to rewrite $f(x)$:\n$$f(x) = 3 - 5\\sin^2 x = 3 - 5(1 - \\cos^2 x) = 3 - 5 + 5\\cos^2 x = 5\\cos^2 x - 2$$\nwhere $a = 5$ and $b = -2$."
